<!-- The Halo 3-style PARTY screen (port/linux/src/p2p_party.h; menu_functions.c "port h3 party
..."): the party's members, the longest-standing first, the leader marked, what each is doing or
why they could not follow the leader; LEAVE PARTY; the party invites waiting. FRIENDS' PARTY row
opens it (the FRIENDS screen's Triangle on a friend invites them: INVITE TO PARTY). Cross on a
member: its options (MUTE or UNMUTE, here only; REMOVE FROM PARTY for the leader); on an invite:
JOIN PARTY (Square: no). Party chat under the list: its newest lines (a member's name as the party
lists show it), Square for QUICK CHAT (presets, no typing), Triangle to type a message (the system's
keyboard on the Vita). The settings panel's Multiplayer > Party does the same for the original
menus (SELECT + D-pad left opens it at once, in play too). The art is this folder's own (tools/halo3_menu_art.py): the FRIENDS screen's. -->
